      "responsibilities": "<p><strong>About the role:</strong></p><p>The role of the Software Engineer is to build high-quality, innovative, and fully performing</p><p>software that complies with coding standards and technical design. We are looking for engineers who lead with <strong>honesty</strong> in their technical ownership, <strong>empathy</strong> for the end-user experience, and the <strong>agility</strong> to navigate both client-side and backend systems.</p><p><br></p><p><strong>What you’ll do (Responsibilities)</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Develop software applications</strong> using programming languages and tools used in software development with the agility to build scalable and reliable solutions.</li><li>Analyze technical problems and propose effective solutions with <strong>honesty</strong> and transparency, seeking guidance when needed.</li><li>Work effectively in a team environment, collaborate with team members, and follow instructions from senior team members or team leads through strong <strong>empathy</strong> and open communication.</li><li>Learn and adapt to new technologies, programming languages, and software development methodologies with high <strong>agility</strong> in a fast-evolving tech stack.</li><li>Maintain quality and attention to detail in software development tasks, backed by an <strong>honest</strong> commitment to clean code.</li><li>Create and document technical specifications, software designs, and coding changes with <strong>honesty</strong> and clarity for seamless team collaboration.</li><li>Adhere to coding standards, software development best practices, and maintain confidentiality of sensitive information with complete <strong>honesty</strong> and integrity.</li></ul>",
      "requirements": "<p><strong>What capabilities you’ll need (Requirements):</strong></p><ul><li>Have experience in software development, with a proven track record of successfully delivering complex software projects through high <strong>agility</strong> and technical excellence.</li><li>Extensive experience and proficiency in <strong>Go or PHP &amp; Angular</strong>, demonstrating the <strong>agility</strong> to work seamlessly across front-end and back-end ecosystems.</li><li>Understanding of software development principles, architecture, design patterns, and best practices applied with <strong>empathy</strong> for long-term code maintainability.</li><li>Familiarity with software development tools and frameworks, version control systems, and bug tracking systems.</li><li>Ability to analyze technical problems, propose effective solutions, and make informed decisions with <strong>honesty</strong> and objectivity.</li><li>Good communication skills with strong <strong>empathy</strong> to effectively convey ideas, listen, and discuss technical concepts with team members.</li><li>Proactive approach to self-learning and self-improvement in the field of software development, driven by continuous <strong>agility</strong>.</li><li>Ability to plan, organize, and manage software development projects—including defining project scope, timeline, and resources—with <strong>agility</strong> to adapt to shifting priorities.</li><li>Commitment to staying up-to-date with the latest advancements in software development technologies, methodologies, and best practices through an <strong>agile</strong> mindset.</li><li>Ability to handle sensitive or confidential information with discretion and strict <strong>honesty</strong>.</li></ul><p><br></p><p><strong>Bonus points if you have the following skills</strong></p><ul><li>Knowledge of multiple programming languages and libraries (Angular, Go, MySQL, Dart, or PHP), showcasing technical <strong>agility</strong> across diverse environments.</li></ul>",
